==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=Euclidean}}

===Alternative spellings===
* [[Euclidian]]

===Etymology===
Named after [[w:Euclid|Euclid]], who established the principles of [[plane geometry]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|US}} {{IPA|/juːˈklɪd.i.ən/}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{geometry}} Adhering to the principles of traditional [[geometry]], in which [[parallel]] [[line]]s are [[equidistant]].
# Of or relating to [[w:Euclid|Euclid]]'s ''[[w:Euclid's Elements|Elements]]'', ''especially'' to [[Euclidean geometry]].

